#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:5
#: 13ad931f09a944d9a6bda849a46f49eb
msgid "Calibration: Radio Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:7
#: d4f060820e5341438b4081c9c242a7a5
msgid "This article explains how to calibrate your autopilot to work with your RC transmitter and receiver. See :ref:`Autopilot calibration <autopilot-calibration>` for other calibration tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:12
#: 11fdcde1389140ae8abe4fbc802d4acc
msgid "1 Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:14
#: 9d83c9b40dcf4ce2a2b8a374ec221b73
msgid "Before performing setup, ensure that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:16
#: 47ddc7360832480db13a6030dae97a7e
msgid "The vehicle is completely built to flight condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:17
#: 0115142b2ec1439b8e06024338756c85
msgid ":ref:`Firmware has been loaded onto the autopilot. <install-firmware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:18
#: cb2e9aa11f564e49aa4f2be9158223e8
msgid ":ref:`Autopilot is connected to APM Planner and connected to Mavlink. <connect-autopilot>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:19
#: 14cbcc22345a4e30970b37af279a3f3b
msgid "RC transmitter and receiver are bound and powered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:20
#: 37362d2a1f2b4c3ba5ab2e9ce95f9fd3
msgid "Propellers are removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:23
#: a7499bc940b7418eba1e345848d92e50
msgid "2 Prepare transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:25
#: 1ac26465fbb347ffa8dc44bddb50ebcd
msgid "Turn on the transmitter, and verify that it is in **airplane mode** (APM needs airplane mode regardless of the platform type being piloted) and all trims are centered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:29
#: bf27e88f2a734f3883c76efd1a289daa
msgid "For Mode 1 transmitters, the left stick will control pitch and yaw, the right stick will control throttle and roll. For Mode 2 transmitters, the left stick will control throttle and yaw; the right stick will control pitch and roll. For either type of transmitter, the transmitter’s three-position switch should be attached to channel 5 and will control flight modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:37
#: 6c585743b5424d4b9c19cca8335957c1
msgid "3 Calibrate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:39
#: 50c00ac602c64c18ae512f7965452ff6
msgid "Select Radio Calibration to teach your autopilot to work with your RC transmitter and receiver. Select **Start Calibration** to begin. Read the instructions in the following prompt and select **OK**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:46
#: 6bf52b0a2df9420fb4186d4ca795f832
msgid "APM Planner2: Radio CalibrationScreen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:48
#: 9eb2e500ee4f4df9ab2ce0a1e91f717a
msgid "Select Start Calibration to begin. Move both sticks in the largest circle possible so that they reach their complete range of motion. Move the Ch 5 and 6 toggle switches through their range of positions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:52
#: aaac00541ce042c8bfe107b51b905eec
msgid "Your transmitter should cause the following control changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:54
#: 9c0b094ff82841579cda7e999c89d55d
msgid "Channel 1: low = roll left, high = roll right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:56
#: d1ecd82a8dcb4f94959ec48e7d463c25
msgid "Channel 2: low = pitch forward, high=pitch back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:58
#: 9c88640f5c3d45569c5bf7cf3e1384eb
msgid "Channel 3: low = throttle down (off), high = throttle up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:60
#: 30ac1c8b77054a6a92ae4b8c548e119d
msgid "Channel 4: low = yaw left, high = yaw right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/radio-calibration.rst:62
#: c0ceced7e450451290863bde3164c70b
msgid "Watch the red bars on the screen to ensure that the correct controls activate for each stick movement. If the red bars move in the opposite direction that you're moving the sticks, you will need to reverse the channel on your transmitter. Select **End Calibration** when complete. Resulting normal values are around 1100 for minimums and 1900 for maximums."
msgstr ""
